# Security rules

## Secrets

- Never commit `.env`, `.env.local`, credentials JSON, or private keys.
- Never log tokens, cookies, or `Authorization` headers — redact in errors.
- Server-only env vars: no `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix for secrets.

## API & webhooks

- Validate all inbound body/query at route boundaries (zod or equivalent).
- Verify webhook signatures (HMAC) before processing; constant-time compare.
- Idempotency keys for webhook handlers that mutate state.

## SSRF

- Do not pass user-controlled URLs to server-side `fetch` without allowlist.
- No arbitrary URL preview or proxy endpoints without validation.

## Authz

- Enforce auth checks on every sensitive mutation, not only UI.
- Server Actions and Route Handlers that change data must verify session/role.

## Dependencies

- Run `pnpm audit` before milestone merge; no unwaived high/critical CVEs.

## Factory hooks

- `guard-secrets.sh` blocks staging `.env` files in git commands.
- Stop hook scans diffs for common secret patterns.
